D).\n6. Which fields each function does and does NOT initialise.\n7. Loop bounds and fall-through semantics (the `switch (len - i)` cascade in stbds_siphash_bytes).\n8. The macro expansions used inside `sh_geti` (shgeti, sh_new_strdup, sh_new_arena, shdefault, shput, shlen, shget, shdel, shfree) — confirm the Rust helper functions expand to exactly the same call sequences and index arithmetic.\n9. The `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)` call: the struct `{char *key; int value;}` is passed BY VALUE in a variadic call. Confirm the Rust equivalent produces identical output under the SysV AMD64 ABI.\n\nFor each function, state either \"MATCHES\" with a one-line justification, or describe the EXACT divergence with C line numbers and Rust line numbers. Be concrete and skeptical; do not assume correctness. Report a final list of any real divergences found (or \"none found\"). Also list anything you consider risky-but-probably-equivalent."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11460,"cache_read_input_tokens":350373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11460,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b643f80a-4a3f-46ec-a182-2be51940f001","uuid":"2650e3de-ea0d-45d4-ae15-cabf5fe70479","timestamp":"2026-08-27T17:21:45.127Z"}
