{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pae5ava24ujjrfjlo42rwtbf377tm6tk62pu3mw2fsy7cs67bzya","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verified against both files (C structs/macros at lines 235-247, 317-350, 360-381; Rust at 65-130, 195-215).\n\n**1. `stbds_siphash_bytes` — MATCHES**\nConstants (`0x736f6d65`/`0x70736575`, `0x646f7261`/`0x6e646f6d`, `0x6c796765`/`0x6e657261`, `0x74656462`/`0x79746573`, `0x0706050403020100`, `0x0f0e0d0c0b0a0908`), `~seed` placement, and `0xff` all identical. `STBDS_ROTATE_LEFT` is a literal transcription (`(val<<n)|(val>>(64-n))`), and the 14 SIPROUND steps are in exact C order with `wrapping_add` for the unsigned `+=`; C/D rounds are 2/4. The two sign-extension traps are handled correctly: the main-loop `data = d[0]|...|(d[3]<<24)` is `int` and sign-extends — reproduced by `c_int_to_size_t` (lines 507-511); the `hi` half is `(size_t)` cast *before* `<<16<<16`, so the sign bits shift out either way. Tail cases 7/6/5 use `(size_t)` casts (shifts 48/40/32, split to dodge the C shift-count limit) and Rust matches; case 4 is *un*cast `int` and Rust correctly wraps it in `c_int_to_size_t` (line 546), while cases 3/2/1 can't go negative and use plain `usize`. Fall-through cascade: since the loop guarantees `len-i ∈ 0..=7`, the descending `if rem >= 7,6,5,4,3,2,1` chain is exactly the C cascade. `data = len << 56` and pointer advance-after-body match.\n\n**2. `stbds_make_hash_index` — MATCHES**\nAlloc size expression, `STBDS_ALIGN_FWD((size_t)(t+1), 64)` (Rust `t.wrapping_add(1)` also strides `size_of::<stbds_hash_index>()`, `#[repr(C)]` field order identical), and all thresholds (`slot_count - (slot_count>>2)`, `(>>3)+(>>4)`, `>>2`, zeroed when `slot_count <= 8`) match. `stbds_load_32_or_64` is unrolled faithfully: in C `0x87b0b0fd`/`0xb504f32d` are `unsigned int` (zero-extend) and `2147001325`/`715136305` are positive `int`, so all operands zero-extend to `size_t` — the plain `usize` literals give bit-identical results, and the `<<16<<16 >>16 >>16` sequence is preserved verbatim. Seed update uses `wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_add`. `STBDS_INDEX_IN_USE` inlined as `>= 0` on `isize`; `goto done` → `break 'done` exits only the `for(;;)` and continues the `j` loop, same as the C label placement. Probe cascade (`pos & 7` start, wrap-around `0..limit` second pass, `pos += step`, `step += 8`, `pos &= slot_count-1`) is in the same order. `temp_key` is left uninitialised in both.\n\n**3. `stbds_stralloc` / `stbds_strreset` — MATCHES**\n`block` is `unsigned char`/`u8` in both, so `>>1` and `++` wrap identically. `512 << (block>>1)`: C's oversized shift compiles to an x86 `shl` masked to 6 bits, which `wrapping_shl` reproduces exactly (and `block <= 23` in practice, so the mask never engages). `BLOCKSIZE_MAX = 1<<20` guard, `sizeof(*sb)-8+len` / `+blocksize`, the `a->storage` non-null splice (`sb->next = a->storage->next`) vs. the null case (`remaining = 0`), and `p = storage + remaining - len` byte arithmetic (`c_char` stride 1) all agree. `strreset` frees the chain then `memset`s the whole arena.\n\n**Conclusion: all three functions are faithful translations; no divergences found.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9757,"cache_read_input_tokens":27567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9757,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01C7J9wGBw246jgtTwSktu2v","session_id":"b643f80a-4a3f-46ec-a182-2be51940f001","uuid":"5a2e99f7-dd16-4938-ac56-ea9e9c74cd73","timestamp":"2026-08-27T17:40:03.396Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review siphash and arena semantics"}
