{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2fxo2hffcepvkzxsbyrnu3rc5gnh4ognc3hycjysnkqbhg5mc7mq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and **no divergence was found — `translation/src/lib.rs` needed no changes** (it is still the original 1348 lines).\n\n## What was done\n\n**Phase A — artifacts** (`translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`)\n- `c_src` is a single translation unit (`lib.c`, 986 lines); all 16 exported `T` symbols exist in both `.so`s, and every `static` C function has a private Rust counterpart. Nothing was missing, so nothing needed translating or stubbing.\n- **ERRORS.md: 66 rows** — every `STBDS_ASSERT`, every early `return`/sentinel, every NULL check, threshold, and min/max constant.\n- **CONFIGS.md: 86 rows** — cross-product of `mode` (incl. `INT_MIN`/`-1`/`2`/`INT_MAX`), `table->string.mode` (incl. out-of-range `4`/`200`/`255`), `elemsize`/`keysize`/`keyoffset`, element counts, slot counts 8→4096, delete shapes, arena states, seeds, and every entry point (not just `sh_geti`).\n\n**Phases B/C/D — 146 tests** (`tests/*.rs`, both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`, never calling Rust directly). Hash-map tests compare the *entire* state after *every* op: array header, every element (dereferencing key pointers), all 11 `stbds_hash_index` fields, the embedded arena, and every bucket's `hash[]`/`index[]` — bit-for-bit, since the global seed is reset identically in both.\n\n## Real C behaviours discovered (my initial ERRORS.md assumptions were wrong; the C is ground truth)\n1. **`stbds_arrgrowf(NULL, es, 0, 0)` returns `NULL`** — `min_cap <= arrcap` is checked *before* the `min_cap < 4` clamp.\n2. **`hmdel_key` with `mode != STBDS_HM_STRING` on a string map aborts.** The swap-with-last re-lookup passes the *element address* instead of the stored `char*`, so `STBDS_ASSERT(slot >= 0)` fires. Both `.so`s die with `SIGABRT` — verified in subprocesses (exit 134 each).\n3. `table->temp_key` is never initialised and only written on two of the four put paths; `sh_geti` prints in *array* order, so its stdout is seed-independent.\n\n## Harness pitfalls I had to fix (not translation bugs)\nUninitialised element value areas, `realloc` addresses being allocator-dependent (replaced with a transcription of the C growth model), dangling caller key pointers under `SH_DEFAULT`, a self-inflicted mutex deadlock, and — found only by repeated *parallel debug* runs — libtest's own progress output leaking into `capture_stdout`, now isolated in a subprocess.\n\n## Gate\n- `nm -D`: 16/16 symbols, 0 missing, 0 extra; `ldd -r` clean on both.\n- ERRORS.md 66/66 ✓, CONFIGS.md 86/86 ✓ (fuzz rows run 3000 randomized sequences each).\n- `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so the full matrix is `default` + `--no-default-features`; `./check_all_features.sh` enumerates the power set automatically and both pass. Also confirmed against a debug-built *and* a release-built cdylib, single-threaded and parallel, over repeated runs.\n\n`c_src/` is byte-for-byte unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":446042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":793,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b643f80a-4a3f-46ec-a182-2be51940f001","uuid":"dfadb2e2-933a-442a-9101-400ddc308052","timestamp":"2026-08-27T17:43:06.795Z"}
